\cf0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>One night, Tony awoke from a fitful sleep of disturbing dreams and felt his consciousness pour into what he believed was yet another dream. An old man, with long grey beard and crazed hair, dressed in full leathers, stood at the foot of his bed. Tony felt no compunction to acknowledge the apparition, until it spoke:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Don\'92t despair, young Tony.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Life\'92s shit, then you lose the only ray of sunshine that\'92s ever blessed your Cloudborne head,\'92 Tony mumbled into his pillow. His eyelids were as heavy as storefront shutters.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tony!\'92 the apparition wheezed, louder than a whisper. \'91Get your shit together. We\'92re depending on you.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony blinked and reappraised the ghost. \'91Hey, don\'92t I know you?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> The ghost stepped to the side of the bed and handed Tony a business card.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I can\'92t read this in the dark,\'92 Tony complained. He was unaccustomed to having a working lamp on a bedside table.\
